HPC deployment guide for Aetheris

1. Target environment

Cluster type: Multi‑node HPC cluster

Nodes:

Macro nodes: high‑core CPUs + GPUs (fluid/N‑body)

Meso nodes: CPU‑heavy, good memory (FEM)

Micro nodes: GPU‑optimized (MD)

Coordinator node: runs U.M.F. + orchestration

Security node: HSM / key management

2. Software stack

OS: Linux (e.g., Ubuntu Server, CentOS, Rocky)

Core tools:

Python 3.x

C++17/20 toolchain (gcc/clang)

MPI (OpenMPI or MPICH)

CUDA / ROCm for GPU nodes

FEM library (FEniCS, deal.II)

MD library (optional: GROMACS/NAMD integration)

Crypto libs (OpenSSL, PQCrypto for Kyber)

Job scheduler (Slurm, PBS, or similar)

3. Codebase layout (cluster‑ready)

Deploy the aetheris/ repo to a shared filesystem:

/aetheris/
  aetheris_core/
  modules/
    astrophysics/
    mechanobiology/
    molecular/
  security/
  deployment/
  scripts/

4. Node role configuration

Create a simple config file, e.g. deployment/cluster_config.yaml:

nodes:
  macro:
    count: 4
    roles: [astrophysics]
  meso:
    count: 3
    roles: [mechanobiology]
  micro:
    count: 4
    roles: [molecular]
  coordinator:
    count: 1
    roles: [umf, scheduler]
  security:
    count: 1
    roles: [encryption, keys]

5. Launch pattern (Slurm example)

5.1 Job script

#!/bin/bash
#SBATCH --job-name=aetheris_full
#SBATCH --nodes=12
#SBATCH --ntasks-per-node=1
#SBATCH --time=24:00:00

module load python cuda mpi

srun python scripts/run_full_simulation.py --config configs/hpc_full.yaml

6. Runtime orchestration

Coordinator node:

Starts U.M.F. router and global scheduler.

Assigns tasks to macro/meso/micro nodes via MPI or gRPC.

Module nodes:

Each node runs its module loop (macro/meso/micro) and exchanges state with U.M.F. at each sync step.

Security node:

Receives snapshots from coordinator.

Encrypts and stores them (AES‑GCM + Kyber).

7. Performance tuning

Macro:

Enable GPU acceleration for N‑body and fluid solvers.

Use domain decomposition for large grids.

Meso:

Optimize FEM mesh partitioning across CPU cores.

Use sparse matrix solvers tuned for the cluster.

Micro:

Batch MD systems per GPU.

Use mixed precision where safe.

Global:

Minimize cross‑node communication frequency.

Use asynchronous snapshotting to avoid blocking.

8. Monitoring and logging

Centralize logs under /aetheris/logs/:

macro.log, meso.log, micro.log, umf.log, security.log.

Use cluster monitoring tools (Prometheus/Grafana, or native HPC tools) to track:

CPU/GPU utilization

memory usage

network bandwidth

job runtime

